  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving food and nutritional security and women`s empowerment in communities of Eastern Chad province of Wadi Fira affected by the Sudan crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to protect, safeguard and strengthen agriculture-based livelihoods (crop production and animal rearing), in order to improve households food and nutrition security, women empowerment and social cohesion among refugees, returnees and host communities affected by the Sudanese crisis, in the Department of Dar-Tama, Province of Wadi Fira, in Eastern Chad. The project will target 700 vulnerable households (4,200 people) including Soudanese refugees and Chadian returnees who have fled the war in Sudan, and their host communities. Since majority of them are women, the project will give a particular attention/priority to women and young girls by promoting their empowerment and enhancing their participation in decision-making related to safeguard their agricultural livelihoods, ensure nutritive food for all family members, as well as promoting peacebuilding and social cohesion in the host community.</narrative>
  </description>
